WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.040
 Yes, this is what you've been waiting for!

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.920
 This is a proper video support

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.720
 that is already in fframes,

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.680
 few minutes from PR merge,

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.440
 but you can see it works.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:12.840
 It already works!

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.560
 It's crazy, it didn't work all this time,

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.240
 but that's why we're in beta.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.800
 And now we are much closer to the public release.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.040
 This video that you see my face from

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.680
 is decoded in runtime and passed as

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.320
 a native SVG image.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:32.200
 So I can do any SVG manipulation if I want to.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.320
 And it just like works out of the box really, really fast.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.200
 Doesn't harm parallelization at all and works in GPU and CPU

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.360
 all the modes and super, super useful.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:46.800
 Very excited about this feature and more to come.

